Run the phase 2 rules when the request body is not inspected.

With SecRequestBodyAccess Off (or ctl:requestBodyAccess=Off), libmodsecurity
v3 returns from Transaction::processRequestBody() before it evaluates the
phase 2 rules, after it has parsed the body all the same. Most of the OWASP
CRS runs in phase 2, including the rules on the request line, the query
string and the headers and the inbound anomaly evaluation (949110), so a
site that inspects no request body was left almost unprotected (upstream
issue owasp-modsecurity/ModSecurity#2465; CRS advisory of 2021-03-02,
"Disabling Request Body Access in ModSecurity 3 Leads to Complete Bypass").

Decide on body access first: without it the body is neither parsed nor
exposed to the rules (no ARGS_POST, FILES, REQUEST_BODY or FULL_REQUEST;
REQBODY_ERROR is 0), and the phase 2 rules run as in ModSecurity v2.

--- a/src/transaction.cc
+++ b/src/transaction.cc
@@ -684,6 +684,37 @@
     }
 
     /*
+     * Without request body access the body is neither parsed nor exposed to
+     * the rules, but the phase 2 rules still run, as in ModSecurity v2: they
+     * also inspect the request line, the query string and the headers
+     * (upstream issue #2465: returning here skipped them all).
+     */
+    bool requestBodyAccess = true;
+    if (m_rules->m_secRequestBodyAccess == RulesSetProperties::FalseConfigBoolean) {
+        if (m_requestBodyAccess != RulesSetProperties::TrueConfigBoolean) {
+            ms_dbg(4, "Request body processing is disabled");
+            requestBodyAccess = false;
+        } else {
+            ms_dbg(4, "Request body processing is disabled, but " \
+                "enabled to this transaction due to ctl:requestBodyAccess " \
+                "action");
+        }
+    } else {
+        if (m_requestBodyAccess == RulesSetProperties::FalseConfigBoolean) {
+            ms_dbg(4, "Request body processing is enabled, but " \
+                "disabled to this transaction due to ctl:requestBodyAccess " \
+                "action");
+            requestBodyAccess = false;
+        }
+    }
+    if (!requestBodyAccess) {
+        m_variableReqbodyError.set("0", m_variableOffset);
+        m_variableReqbodyProcessorError.set("0", m_variableOffset);
+        this->m_rules->evaluate(modsecurity::RequestBodyPhase, this);
+        return true;
+    }
+
+    /*
      * Process the request body even if there is nothing to be done.
      *
      * if (m_requestBody.tellp() <= 0) {
@@ -822,24 +853,6 @@
